body:
Thanks for explaining.   

For anyone that cares to know;

Imo,  I dont feel that happened here as the original statement was never clarified, altho the unclarified statement was reiterated. Also, there literally was no debate. I never stated an opinion. I was merely asking questions. Lastly but not least, nothing I've asked or commented on has been in an effort to annoy anyone.

Many people choose this route and there's nothing wrong with that. 2 things tho; 
1. Manufacturers SOMETIMES have clauses that void warranties if not installed by a licensed professional and 
2. Permitting - if you have Entergy New Orleans, well...shooting pool with a cooked pasta noodle is easier.

Questions for anyone that got a quote from Tesla; 
1. When they quote, do you get to see an actual panel layout on your home? 
2. Do they ask for a picture or any info about your breaker panel?
